{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"?<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"text"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"S","preciseIdentifier":"s:SdySdSgxcSyRzlufc1SL_xmfp"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/StringProtocol","text":"StringProtocol","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sy"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"parameters":[{"name":"text","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An input string to convert to a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double?","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The string passed as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" can represent a real number in decimal or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hexadecimal format or can be in a special format representing infinity"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or NaN (“not a number”). If "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" is not in a recognized format,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the optional initializer will fail and return "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" string consists of an optional"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plus or minus sign character ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"+"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"followed by one of the following:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"decimal string","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" contains a significand consisting of one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or more decimal digits that may include a decimal point:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let c = Double(\"-1.0\")","\/\/ c == -1.0","","let d = Double(\"28.375\")","\/\/ d == 28.375"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A decimal string may also include an exponent following the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"significand, indicating the power of 10 by which the significand should"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be multiplied. If included, the exponent is separated by a single"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"character, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"e"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"E"},{"type":"text","text":", and consists of an optional plus or minus sign"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"character and a sequence of decimal digits."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let e = Double(\"2837.5e-2\")","\/\/ e == 28.375"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"hexadecimal string","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" contains a significand consisting of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0X"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0x"},{"type":"text","text":" followed by one or more hexadecimal digits that may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"include a decimal point."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let f = Double(\"0x1c.6\")","\/\/ f == 28.375"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A hexadecimal string may also include an exponent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indicating the power of 2 by which the significand should"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be multiplied. If included, the exponent is separated by a single"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"character, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"P"},{"type":"text","text":", and consists of an optional plus or minus sign"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"character and a sequence of decimal digits."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let g = Double(\"0x1.c6p4\")","\/\/ g == 28.375"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The input strings "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"inf\""},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"infinity\""},{"type":"text","text":" (case insensitive)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are converted to an infinite result:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let i = Double(\"inf\")","\/\/ i == Double.infinity","","let j = Double(\"-Infinity\")","\/\/ j == -Double.infinity"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An input string of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"nan\""},{"type":"text","text":" (case insensitive) is converted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"into a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"NaN","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" value:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let n = Double(\"-nan\")","\/\/ n?.isNaN == true","\/\/ n?.sign == .minus"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A NaN string may also include a payload in parentheses following the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"typ